/**
 * @mainpage OpenTLV C API reference
 *
 * OpenTLV is an allocation-free TLV library. Public headers define the
 * ownership, lifetime, error and output-preservation contracts below.
 * Start with the API groups or browse the file and data structure indexes.
 *
 * This reference covers all shipped C builtins, including those
 * disabled in a particular library build. Configuration and version values
 * describe the CMake build used to generate this reference.
 *
 * This reference is part of the OpenTLV documentation site. Read the
 * @docs{getting-started,getting started guide}, the
 * @docs{concepts/architecture,architecture overview} and the
 * @docs{guides/memory,memory ownership guide} alongside it, and see the
 * @docs{reference/c-api,C API overview} for each area's matching guides.
 * The C++ wrappers are documented in the @docs{reference/cxx-api,C++ API reference}.
 */

/** @defgroup core Core types and utilities
 * Tags, lengths, values, views, byte order, errors and build metadata.
 * Guides: @docs{concepts/core-types,C core types}, @docs{concepts/value,borrowed values} and @docs{guides/memory,memory ownership}.
 */
/** @defgroup diagnostics Diagnostics
 * Structured diagnostic model shared across OpenTLV layers: a stable code, severity, location and
 * nested context, independent of any wire format or protocol.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/diagnostics,diagnostics}.
 */
/** @defgroup reader Reader
 * Canonical pull-based cursor and single-element decoding over borrowed input.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/reader,pull-based reading}, @docs{formats,formats}.
 */
/** @defgroup writer Writer
 * Encoding and stateful output into caller-owned buffers.
 * Guides: @docs{formats,formats}, @docs{guides/writer,bounded Tree Writer}.
 */
/** @defgroup traversal Traversal
 * Traversing adjacent or nested elements through the canonical Reader cursor.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/reader,pull-based reading}.
 */
/** @defgroup schemas Schemas
 * Structural validation and schema-driven encoding.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/schemas,schemas and length validation}.
 */
/** @defgroup codecs Codecs
 * Value conversion and structured codecs, including EMV values.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/codecs,value codecs}.
 */
/** @defgroup field_encoding Field Encoding
 * Reusable callbacks and fixed-width, packed, variable-width and escaped wire-field primitives.
 * These primitives encode individual fields; Format composition defines complete element framing.
 * Guides: @docs{formats,formats}.
 */
/** @defgroup formats Formats
 * Format callbacks, composition and default, fixed, BER, DER and CER wire formats.
 * Guides: @docs{formats,formats}.
 */
/** @defgroup builtins Builtins
 * DER and CER validation, EMV dictionaries and DOL utilities.
 * Guides: @docs{standards/emv,EMV}, @docs{standards/der,DER} and @docs{standards/cer,CER}.
 */
/** @defgroup copy Copy utilities
 * Copying views and encoded bytes into caller-owned storage.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/copy,copy helpers}.
 */
/** @defgroup document Mutable document
 * Optional owned tree of elements that can be searched, changed and encoded again; the only allocating component.
 * Guides: @docs{guides/document,mutable documents}.
 */
